WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.792
The wavy edge passes through the windows in both blue wafers.

00:00:01.792 --> 00:00:03.458
As the handle rocks, the far end of the blade rises and falls inside the rear wafer.

00:00:03.458 --> 00:00:04.375
The copper teeth hold both wafers. The rear tip is still in the brass slot, so the turn stops.

00:00:04.375 --> 00:00:09.000
The picker eases the turn. Small strokes of the blade lift the wafers and let their springs push them back down.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:09.500
During this stroke the blade brings both wafer tips clear of the brass. The teeth line up on both bars.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.000
The teeth grip with both tips clear. The blade carries the plug past the point where it caught before.
